snapshot:" line stops advancing; the back's first "Native MME DMA read fifoed start=0x142" lines
and its "Native MME render enable modes" line every few seconds (front macros never logged them).
Readouts: walk fps mean and 1% low, flashes/min (render enable decisions now on the back), pond
load OK; SPLIT_WAITS front waited, back idle, list writers, acquire check; the #1056 line's back
run time and "while it still had work queued"; the control's list counts (T84's vs LISTSYNC's vs
#1056's vs #1055's verdicts); ml: waited and "found GPU-written by the second look"; no "command
entry ... was GPU-written by work queued before it" line in any arm. v: "Split front register
checks: N done, 0 differences". m wins only if it beats the same-batch controls in both batches,
flashes/min are not higher, and back idle fell by more than the #1056 line's back run time (under
the full frame wait the back is the frame's long pole: a busier back with no fewer gaps is a loss).

